,"setting":["ziklag","brook_besor"],"on_stage_named":["david","abiathar"],"on_stage_unnamed":["amalekite_youth","israelites"],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"30:21","end":"30:31","title":"Division of plunder and gifts to Judah","setting":["ziklag"],"on_stage_named":["david"],"on_stage_unnamed":["israelites"],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"31:1","end":"31:6","title":"Death of Saul and his sons","setting":["mount_gilboa"],"on_stage_named":["saul","jonathan","abinadab"],"on_stage_unnamed":["saul_armorbearer","philistines"],"mentioned_only":[]},{"start":"31:7","end":"31:13","title":"Bodies of Saul and sons recovered","setting":["mount_gilboa","beth_shan","jabesh_gilead"],"on_stage_named":["saul"],"on_stage_unnamed":["philistines","jabesh_men"],"mentioned_only":[]}],"brief":{"era":"Late Bronze to early Iron Age, c. 11th century BCE, the transition from judges to monarchy in Israel","place":"Hill country of Ephraim and Benjamin, Shiloh, Gibeah, Philistine cities (Ashdod, Gath, Ekron), the wilderness of Judah and Ziph, En Gedi, and Ziklag","dress":"Priests wear linen ephods; Samuel as a child wears a linen ephod and small robe; Saul is tall and dressed as a royal warrior; Philistine warriors wear bronze helmets and coats of mail; Israelite shepherds and women wear simple tunics and head coverings","buildings_and_objects":"Tabernacle at Shiloh with doorposts and gates; the ark of the covenant with cherubim; Dagon's temple in Ashdod; Philistine cart drawn by milk cows; bronze armor; sling and five smooth stones; harp and spear of Saul; oil horn for anointing; tambourines and lutes; caves and rocky crags of the wilderness; a tamarisk tree at Gibeah","depiction_rules":["Yahweh is never depicted as a human figure; show only the ark, voice, light, thunder, or an unseen presence","The ark of the covenant is a sacred object and should be shown without any human face within it","Samuel's apparition at Endor should be depicted as a spirit or old man in a robe rising from the earth, not a demon","The divine spirit and evil spirit should appear as an invisible force, not as a figure","Dagon should be shown as a fallen idol, not a living god","Avoid graphic depiction of the massacre at Nob and the killing of Agag; show the aftermath or the act in shadow"]}}}